silm:instances_papers_07_the_canonical_question_chapters_01_answerability_profile_sections_04_answerability_audit_yoneda_hom_leg_2 silm:hasExample "In 'P07AnswerabilityProfileAnswerabilityAuditYonedaHomLeg2', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, Felis catus / TSN 183798 is the ITIS taxonomy source row admitting the cat-classification arrow into D_Mittens; it is a source leg, not the cat." .
